<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5610" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bŏvillus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., a very ancient form of the class. bubulus [bos].
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>pertaining to oxen</i>
			or <i>cows</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grex, in an old religious formula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					22, 10, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carnes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Theod. Prisc. 1, 7</span></i>
			.—No <i>comp.</i> or <i>sup.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bŏvillus</span></b> , a,
				um, = Bovillanus; v. Bovillae, I. B. 1. <i>fin.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
